  data: {
    LLM: "Always raise with a pair or better. Always fold with less than A-K. With A-K hand, raise if dealer's face-up card is A or K and you hold another A or K in hand.\n\nOptimal strategy: Raise with pair or better always. Fold with less than A-K. With A-K high: raise if dealer's up-card matches any of your other 4 cards.\n\nHouse edge cannot be eliminated. The progressive jackpot side bet has very poor EV unless jackpot is extremely high (~$200,000+ for break-even on $1 bet with royal flush). Basic strategy reduces house edge from ~5.7% to ~5.2%.",
    Player: "Always raise with a pair or better. Always fold with less than A-K. With A-K hand, raise if dealer's face-up card is A or K and you hold another A or K in hand.\n\nOptimal strategy: Raise with pair or better always. Fold with less than A-K. With A-K high: raise if dealer's up-card matches any of your other 4 cards.\n\nHouse edge cannot be eliminated. The progressive jackpot side bet has very poor EV unless jackpot is extremely high (~$200,000+ for break-even on $1 bet with royal flush). Basic strategy reduces house edge from ~5.7% to ~5.2%.",
